# NOTICE — provenance and redaction

This repository is a **curated sibling set**, not a claim that every `SKILL.md` body is original to the publisher.

## Third-party / upstream skill bodies

Several Godot skills were selected from the TBS / game-dev on-demand pack, which itself vendors community sources. Treat those bodies as **upstream-attributed**, not original essays. Many expansion siblings are community / vendor skills copied from a private library after an independent quality pass.

| Skill cluster | Upstream (when known) | Notes |
|---------------|------------------------|-------|
| `godot-*` (most v1 slices) | [gd-agentic-skills](https://github.com/thedivergentai/gd-agentic-skills) | Deep Godot 4 procedures |
| `godot-ui` | [awesome-gamedev-agent-skills](https://github.com/gamedev-skills/awesome-gamedev-agent-skills) (`godot-ui-control`) | Control-node UI hub |
| `game-godot`, `game-csharp-godot`, `godot-gdscript-mastery` | community / open research copies | Hub + C# + idioms (patterns twin cut) |
| `systematic-debugging` | adapted from obra/superpowers (MIT) | Frontmatter records the adaptation |
| `web-interface-guidelines` | Vercel web-interface guidance restated as a skill | Not an official Vercel product |
| `senior-frontend` | community frontend skill | React / Next / Tailwind |
| Vendor chairs (Vercel, Expo, Neon, shadcn, …) | Their public skill repos when `source` is a GitHub URL | Prefer upstream for latest |
| `weaviate` | [weaviate/agent-skills](https://github.com/weaviate/agent-skills) | BSD-3-Clause; client pin checked against docs.weaviate.io (v4.22) |

If an upstream license is Apache-2.0 (some Godot UI metadata says so), that file's header wins for that folder. The repo-level license is MIT for **original** docs and original agent-OS chairs.

**Do not assume every body is original.** Prefer the upstream repo when you need the latest vendor-true copy.

## last30days (not vendored)

This repo does **not** ship [mvanhorn/last30days-skill](https://github.com/mvanhorn/last30days-skill). That engine is MIT, ~53k stars, and would be dishonest to re-host here. Install it yourself (`npx skills add mvanhorn/last30days-skill -g`). Attribution: mvanhorn, MIT.

## What was redacted

Before this tree was published, copies were scrubbed of:

- Personal Windows profile paths (`C:\Users\<name>` → `~/`)
- Private vault / cloud-drive roots
- Owner email addresses (replaced with `user@example.com` where an example address was required)
- Machine-only runtime paths and account labels

A remaining `sk-` substring in English words such as `task-shaped` or `ask-before` is **not** an API key. Live token prefixes were removed from docs. Secret-scanner examples may mention PAT *shapes* without live tokens.

## What this repo is not

- Not a private-library dump
- Not nested pack parents (`skills/godot/<skill>` is gone; use `skills/godot-ui`)
- Not offensive / dual-use exploit content
- Not affiliated with Anthropic, Cursor, Godot, Vercel, or mvanhorn

The published tree is redacted; git history of earlier commits is not rewritten.
